# Data licence

**This one is genuinely CC-BY-4.0, and here is why — which the previous version
of this file never said.**

## What the sources say

Both sources declare the same grant:

```
wa.minedex.sites     Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (WA SLIP public services)
wa.tenements.live    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (WA SLIP public services)
                     https://catalogue.data.wa.gov.au/
```

Western Australia publishes these through SLIP under CC BY 4.0. CC BY permits
redistribution under the same licence, so passing it through is exactly what the
grant contemplates — unlike most of this fleet, where the boilerplate was
asserting rights nobody had granted.

## What this repository grants

| what | licence |
| --- | --- |
| the code | MIT, see [LICENSE](LICENSE) |
| `derived/`, `raw/`, `manifest/` | **CC BY 4.0**, passed through from WA SLIP |

## Attribution, which CC BY requires

Attribute the **Government of Western Australia (Department of Mines, Industry
Regulation and Safety)** as the source, and say that you obtained it via this
repository rather than implying the State endorses your use. Link the catalogue
entry above. Attribution is a licence condition here, not a courtesy.

